WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.072
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:08.920
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:15.832
Unit twenty-one: Sleep and Rest. In this unit, you will explain why sleep is important and give advice.

4
00:00:16.817 --> 00:00:17.620
Sleep.

5
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.784
Sleep means to rest with your eyes closed.

6
00:00:21.084 --> 00:00:23.444
Children should sleep for nine or ten hours.

7
00:00:24.144 --> 00:00:26.831
Your turn. Say: Sleep.

8
00:00:29.531 --> 00:00:30.265
Sleep.

9
00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:32.100
Rest.

10
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.427
Rest means a time when you relax and do not work.

11
00:00:35.727 --> 00:00:37.947
After football, I need some rest.

12
00:00:38.647 --> 00:00:41.798
Your turn. Say: Rest.

13
00:00:44.498 --> 00:00:45.267
Rest.

14
00:00:46.283 --> 00:00:47.087
Tired.

15
00:00:47.787 --> 00:00:49.775
Tired means needing sleep or rest.

16
00:00:50.075 --> 00:00:51.970
I feel tired in the afternoon.

17
00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.939
Your turn. Say: Tired.

18
00:00:57.639 --> 00:00:58.431
Tired.

19
00:00:59.417 --> 00:01:00.406
Bedtime.

20
00:01:01.106 --> 00:01:03.582
Bedtime means the time you usually go to bed.

21
00:01:03.882 --> 00:01:05.835
My bedtime is nine o'clock.

22
00:01:06.535 --> 00:01:08.990
Your turn. Say: Bedtime.

23
00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:12.656
Bedtime.

24
00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:14.512
Screen.

25
00:01:15.212 --> 00:01:18.918
Screen means the flat part of a phone, TV or computer.

26
00:01:19.218 --> 00:01:21.032
Turn off your screen before bed.

27
00:01:21.732 --> 00:01:24.349
Your turn. Say: Screen.

28
00:01:27.049 --> 00:01:27.969
Screen.

29
00:01:28.983 --> 00:01:29.775
Routine.

30
00:01:30.475 --> 00:01:33.520
Routine means the things you usually do in the same order.

31
00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.203
My bedtime routine is bath, book, bed.

32
00:01:36.903 --> 00:01:39.636
Your turn. Say: Routine.

33
00:01:42.336 --> 00:01:43.186
Routine.

34
00:01:44.183 --> 00:01:44.975
Energy.

35
00:01:45.675 --> 00:01:47.814
Energy means the power to be active.

36
00:01:48.114 --> 00:01:49.870
Good sleep gives me energy.

37
00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.828
Your turn. Say: Energy.

38
00:01:55.528 --> 00:01:56.447
Energy.

39
00:01:57.450 --> 00:01:58.335
Hours.

40
00:01:59.035 --> 00:02:01.220
Hours means periods of sixty minutes.

41
00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.195
I sleep for nine hours.

42
00:02:03.895 --> 00:02:06.849
Your turn. Say: Hours.

43
00:02:09.549 --> 00:02:10.422
Hours.

44
00:02:11.417 --> 00:02:13.405
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:13.705 --> 00:02:16.006
Sreypich, you look tired today.

46
00:02:17.317 --> 00:02:19.873
I played games on my phone until midnight.

47
00:02:21.183 --> 00:02:23.612
It's important to sleep for nine or ten hours.

48
00:02:24.917 --> 00:02:28.266
I know. It's important to turn off the screen too.

49
00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.039
What's your new plan?

50
00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:36.291
My bedtime is nine o'clock. I'll read a book, not my phone!

51
00:02:37.583 --> 00:02:40.639
Grammar focus: It's important to plus verb.

52
00:02:40.939 --> 00:02:42.753
It's important to sleep well.

53
00:02:43.053 --> 00:02:45.494
Use 'It's important to...' to give strong advice.

54
00:02:46.483 --> 00:02:48.973
Now read and listen. Good Night, Good Day.

55
00:02:49.273 --> 00:02:51.702
Sleep gives our body and brain energy.

56
00:02:53.017 --> 00:02:56.537
Children need about nine to ten hours of sleep every night.

57
00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:01.092
It's important to turn off screens one hour before bedtime.

58
00:03:02.383 --> 00:03:05.973
A calm routine, like reading a book, helps us sleep well.

59
00:03:07.283 --> 00:03:10.200
When we rest well, we feel happy and learn better.

60
00:03:11.517 --> 00:03:14.308
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:14.608 --> 00:03:16.387
It's important blank sleep well.

62
00:03:16.687 --> 00:03:19.354
A, to. B, for. C, that.

63
00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:24.943
The answer is A: to.

64
00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.833
The time you usually go to bed is your blank.

65
00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:33.668
A, bedtime. B, routine. C, energy.

66
00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:39.880
The answer is A: bedtime.

67
00:03:41.383 --> 00:03:43.580
Needing sleep or rest is blank.

68
00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:47.058
A, tired. B, calm. C, confident.

69
00:03:51.050 --> 00:03:53.177
The answer is A: tired.

70
00:03:54.683 --> 00:03:57.638
Now it's your turn to speak. Why is sleep important?

71
00:04:02.938 --> 00:04:08.655
Sleep gives us energy. It's important to sleep for nine hours and to turn off screens before bedtime.

72
00:04:08.955 --> 00:04:10.745
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:16.364
Great work today! You learned eight new words and it's important to plus verb.

74
00:04:16.664 --> 00:04:21.929
Today's value is healthy habits. Sleep well, eat well and move every day.

75
00:04:22.229 --> 00:04:24.986
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

76
00:04:25.286 --> 00:04:28.321
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

